00:14:30,159 --> 00:14:36,000
other. And I don't want to have to deal with this because it will be tricky to remember, yeah, maybe

194
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:41,039
this one has a bigger value, this one has less value, I need to give more importance to this or

195
00:14:41,039 --> 00:14:46,000
to that. So what I would do is that I will normalize my vector. It's something that you always do when

196
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:52,399
you do machine learnings and all of those stuff, that is you normalize all your value, all of your

197
00:14:52,399 --> 00:15:01,039
values inside of your features. And to normalize them, basically, you take the average, the

198
00:15:01,039 --> 00:15:05,759
mean of all your values, you subtract the mean, so all your values, if they were all

199
00:15:05,759 --> 00:15:13,360
from zero to 20, then you will switch, you will slide your window to be around zero.

200
00:15:14,319 --> 00:15:19,759
And then you divide all the values by the standard deviations. So the goal is to have

201
00:15:19,759 --> 00:15:26,000
for all of your feature to have a mean of zero and a standard deviation of one.

202
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:30,919
So basically everything now is in the same space, everything has the same

203
00:15:30,919 --> 00:15:34,759
importance and when you try to do an Euclidean distance on the flat vector

204
00:15:34,759 --> 00:15:40,879
like this, it would work. So this is what you do. You take the feature mean, the

